p down on actual vote request\") }\n    phase = \"return\"\n    campaign(1)\n    if len(append2) == 0 { t.Fatal(\"no replacement storage request reached follower\") }\n    observe := func(at string) {\n        logTerm, err := nodes[2].raft.raftLog.term(selectedIndex)\n        if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n        storedTerm, err := stores[2].Term(selectedIndex)\n        if err != nil { t.Fatal(err) }\n        u := &nodes[2].raft.raftLog.unstable\n        emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"view\", \"op\":\"replacement\", \"phase\":at, \"node\":2,\n            \"entry_index\":selectedIndex, \"original_entry_term\":selectedTerm,\n            \"log_term\":logTerm, \"stored_term\":storedTerm, \"raft_term\":nodes[2].BasicStatus().Term,\n            \"unstable_offset\":u.offset, \"unstable_entries\":len(u.entries),\n            \"pending_writes\":len(append2), \"pending_completions\":len(completion2)})\n    }\n    observe(\"before_old_completion\")\n    // Local responses to node 2 retain their production order. Network\n    // responses to other recipients can be delivered while these are delayed.\n    step(completion2[0])\n    completion2 = completion2[1:]\n    observe(\"after_old_completion\")\n    for _, m := range completion2 { step(m) }\n    completion2 = nil\n    deferCompletion2 = false\n    // Finish every delayed request in append-target order before accepting\n    // further work. The current replacement becomes visible in Storage here.\n    for _, m := range append2 { perform(2, m) }\n    append2 = nil\n    observe(\"after_current_completion\")\n    phase = \"finish\"\n    pump()\n    // A finite explicit heartbeat prompts retransmission of previously lost\n    // network traffic; no timer or eventual-commit assumption is an oracle.\n    for i := 0; i < 2; i++ { nodes[1].Tick(); pump() }\n    emit(map[string]interface{}{\"event\":\"finished\", \"op\":\"replacement\",\n        \"pending_network\":len(network), \"pending_append2\":len(append2),\n        \"pending_completion2\":len(completion2), \"dropped_network\":dropped,\n        \"follower_applied\":nodes[2].BasicStatus().Applied, \"follower_commit\":nodes[2].BasicStatus().Commit})\n}\nGO\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json\ns=dict(action='explore',question='Can a delayed original append completion change the follower log view to an intervening conflicting stored entry after a later actual leader has restored the original entry in unstable memory, while replacement storage work remains pending?',rationale='Extend the actual-producer history to five RawNodes and three leadership terms. Keep append-worker requests FIFO. After writes, delay local completion responses to node 2 in FIFO order while delivering durable responses to other recipients. Elect an intervening leader using nodes 3,4,5 without replicating its new entry to 4,5; then reelect node 1 using 1,4,5. Actual rejection/retry messages restore node 1 history at node 2; delay only the resulting replacement writes. Compare the log view against storage before and after the first old completion, then finish all pending work. Device durability is substituted by MemoryStorage without crashes; the driver mutates no raft internals. This addresses the missing competing-write premise, not global consensus safety.',harness_path='storage_replacement_explore_test.go',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['094ea077ebb340d39d82022bc7e733ad','src_raw_append','src_raw_storage_tail','src_async_delivery','src_unstable_role'],answered='Exploration 094ea077ebb340d39d82022bc7e733ad completed with exit 0. Actual term-2 entry index 3 at node 2 remained unstable at offset 3 after a delayed term-2 completion arrived in term 3; the term-3 append request carried zero entries and its completion advanced offset to 4 with no unstable entries. The final driver event reported no pending network or held append work. These observations establish the generated term-only reconfirmation path under the specific in-memory caller policy, not a formal property result.',remaining=['The first exploration had no intervening conflicting stored version. Determine whether delayed completion retains the current unstable view when Storage temporarily contains another term at the same index.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='The existing producer path works, so the next experiment adds exactly the missing competing-write premise. Responses to the same local recipient stay FIFO; responses to different recipients may progress independently after their writes. No prior exploration is relabeled as evidence.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_16-15-15-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"c837c216fcd3487e827915c0a1b1ee96\", \"audit_spec_version\": 2, \"elapsed_seconds\": 1183.6848939709998, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Validation against the state and bytes read; this is not acceptance, execution or evidence\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
